course: dictionary
lesson: 434
title: Arcade in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An arcade can mean a few different things, so the words around it are your clues. «Pong, from Atari in 1972, was the first big hit arcade game.» The word game tells you this arcade is a place with games, and the games are played for coins or tokens.
explain: «Who made the first video game is argued: "Tennis for Two" ran on an oscilloscope in 1958.» Here the clue is video game and the years, so arcade is about games people play in public places, not at home. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "the first big hit place with games you pay for" makes sense.
explain: Buildings can also have arcades. If a sentence talks about arches, a row of curved shapes, or a covered walk with shops, the word means something different. Always ask: what does the sentence say around the word?
fact: An arcade is a place with games you play using coins or tokens.
fact: An arcade can also be a covered passage with shops along it, like a shopping arcade.
fact: In buildings, an arcade is a row of arches.
fact: «Pong», from Atari in 1972, was the first big hit arcade game.
fact: «Spacewar!» ran on a computer in 1962, and «Tennis for Two» ran on an oscilloscope in 1958.
exercise: «Pong, from Atari in 1972, was the first big hit arcade game.» What kind of place is an arcade here? | A bus stop | A row of arches in a church | A place to buy shoes | *A place with games you play using coins or tokens
exercise: Dad says, «Let's walk through the shopping arcade.» What is the arcade? | A game you play with tokens | A bus stop | A row of arches in a wall | *A covered passage with shops along it
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Pong, from Atari in 1972, was the first big hit arcade game» that tells you the arcade has games. | Pong | 1972 | *game | Atari
test: «The stone arcade ran along the front of the old palace.» What does arcade mean here? | A shop for sweets | A game you play with coins | *A row of arches | A bus stop
test: «Spacewar!» ran on a computer in 1962, and Pong came in 1972. How many years after Spacewar! was Pong? | 5 | 12 | 20 | *10
exam: Which meaning fits «The arcade was full of flashing lights and the sound of coins dropping»? | *A place with games you play using coins or tokens | A covered passage with shops along it | A row of arches in a church | A type of bus stop
